{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774300477,"nonce":"5gpjOuwD4LSgbdwcWZnaBSq5RcY=","message":"## Implementation Spec — Backend Figure API Endpoints\n\n### Overview\nNew file `feedbax/web/api/figures.py` with 4 endpoints + router registration in `app.py`.\n\n### Database Access\nUse `db_session()` context manager from `feedbax.database` for all queries. Query `FigureRecord` and `EvaluationRecord` via SQLAlchemy ORM.\n\n### Endpoints\n\n**1. `GET /api/figures`** — List/search figures with pagination\n- Query params: `evaluation_hash`, `expt_name`, `figure_type`, `identifier` (partial match via LIKE), `pert_type`, `pert_std`, `date_from`, `date_to`, `limit` (default 50), `offset` (default 0)\n- Joins `EvaluationRecord` for `expt_name` filtering\n- Excludes archived figures by default\n- Returns: `FigureListResponse` with items (list of `FigureInfo`) + total count + limit + offset\n- `FigureInfo` includes all FigureRecord fields + `expt_name` from eval + available file URLs\n\n**2. `GET /api/figures/{figure_hash}`** — Single figure metadata\n- Returns: `FigureDetail` (full FigureRecord data + expt_name + available_files list)\n- 404 if not found\n\n**3. `GET /api/figures/{figure_hash}/file`** — Serve figure file\n- Query param: `format` (default `json` for Plotly interactive)\n- Content types: json-\u003eapplication/json, html-\u003etext/html, png-\u003eimage/png, svg-\u003eimage/svg+xml, webp-\u003eimage/webp, pdf-\u003eapplication/pdf\n- Uses `FileResponse` for binary, `Response` for json/html\n- 404 if file not found, 400 if format not in saved_formats\n\n**4. `GET /api/figures/evaluations`** — Distinct evaluations with figure counts\n- Returns: list of `EvaluationFigureSummary` (evaluation_hash, expt_name, figure_count, latest_figure_date)\n- Groups by evaluation_hash, ordered by latest figure date desc\n\n### Pydantic Models\nDefined inline in figures.py (matching the pattern in trajectories.py where models are simple).\n\n### Router Registration\nAdd `from feedbax.web.api import figures` and `app.include_router(figures.router, prefix='/api/figures', tags=['figures'])` in `app.py`.","files":null}]}